          "guid": "mrx6w2w98zdsjy5f",
          "message": {
            "text": "The pre-start deliberately does NOT live in the terminal-spawn path the ticket suggested: `attach` → `spawnIntoSession` is fully synchronous (called from the WS message handler), so an in-line daemon start would either block the attach or ripple async through the registry. Pre-starting at project registration (this hook) + `ai_tool` change + drive re-enable achieves a strictly better outcome — the daemon is up long before any terminal resolves, so even the FIRST post-reboot terminal launches attached with zero added latency. \"Warm the thread\" (the ticket's optional half) was investigated and dropped: a freshly restarted daemon loads a thread's rollout from disk on `thread/resume` (live-verified on 0.145.0 by stopping/starting the daemon and resuming a pre-existing thread). See also `src/codexAppServer.ts` (`prestartCodexDaemonIfNeeded` conditions) and `src/codexDaemonTransport.ts` (`ensureCodexDaemonRunning` in-flight dedupe for concurrent project registrations).\n",
            "markdown": "The pre-start deliberately does NOT live in the terminal-spawn path the ticket suggested: `attach` → `spawnIntoSession` is fully synchronous (called from the WS message handler), so an in-line daemon start would either block the attach or ripple async through the registry. Pre-starting at project registration (this hook) + `ai_tool` change + drive re-enable achieves a strictly better outcome — the daemon is up long before any terminal resolves, so even the FIRST post-reboot terminal launches attached with zero added latency. \"Warm the thread\" (the ticket's optional half) was investigated and dropped: a freshly restarted daemon loads a thread's rollout from disk on `thread/resume` (live-verified on 0.145.0 by stopping/starting the daemon and resuming a pre-existing thread). See also `src/codexAppServer.ts` (`prestartCodexDaemonIfNeeded` conditions) and `src/codexDaemonTransport.ts` (`ensureCodexDaemonRunning` in-flight dedupe for concurrent project registrations).\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/terminals/eagerSpawn.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 22,
                  "endLine": 28,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "export function eagerSpawnTerminals(secret: string, dataDir: string): void {\n  // HS-9396 (docs/123 §123.5) — fire-and-forget daemon pre-start for codex\n  // projects with a resumable driven thread, so terminals opened later (lazy\n  // included) resolve to the ATTACHED command without waiting for a play.\n  // Called at exactly the right moments (project registration + terminals\n  // settings changes); a no-op for every other project.\n  try { prestartCodexDaemonIfNeeded(dataDir); } catch { /* best-effort */ }"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
